  "articleBody": "Texas weather can be pretty rough on roofs, from intense sun to sudden, severe storms. When your roof experiences a major event, knowing how to assess the damage is crucial for protecting your home. It’s not just about what you can see from the ground; major damage can affect more than just the surface. You'll want to check for obvious signs like missing shingles or visible punctures, but also consider interior impacts like leaks or ceiling stains.\n\nWhen a significant event impacts your roof, a thorough assessment needs to go beyond surface-level observations. Consider whether the damage is limited to just the shingles or if it might extend to the underlying decking and even structural components. This is especially important for determining if your home remains habitable or safe to enter. Don't forget to look inside, too – check ceilings, floors, and windows for any signs of water intrusion or stress. Documenting everything with photos before any temporary repairs is a smart move.\n\n### What to Expect During the Process\nWhen you call in professionals like Discounted Roofing Co., they'll start by ensuring the area is safe for inspection. They'll meticulously document the date and suspected cause of the damage, taking photos of both exterior and interior issues. Their inspection will cover all critical areas: roof slopes, flashings, penetrations, gutters, and, where safely accessible, attic spaces, decking, and structural elements. A key part of this process is distinguishing between new, event-related damage and any pre-existing wear on your roof. This comprehensive approach helps ensure nothing is missed, giving you a clear picture of your roof's condition.\n\nYour roof is a critical protector of your home, and major damage can be overwhelming. Getting a professional, honest assessment helps you understand the true scope of the problem. It allows you to make informed decisions about repairs or replacement and navigate any insurance claims with confidence.\n\nReady for an expert assessment? Contact Discounted Roofing Co. today for a thorough inspection and honest guidance.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}